    "chapter": "Magic Items",
    "section": "10.28",
    "heading": "Sentient Magic Items",
    "lineStart": 14698,
    "lineEnd": 14704
  },
  "section": "10.28",
  "rulesText": "Some magic items have sentience and personality. Such an item might be possessed, haunted by the spirit of a previous owner, or self-aware thanks to the magic used to create it. A sentient item might be a cherished ally to its wielder or a continual thorn in the side.\n\nMost sentient items are weapons, but other kinds of items can manifest sentience. Single-use items such as potions and scrolls are never sentient.\n\nThe GM controls sentient magic items and their activated properties. A bearer who maintains a good relationship with the item can access those properties. If the relationship is strained, a conflict can ensue (see “Conflict” below)."
}
